  "scope": "Game 12 decision 15. Both policies select moves from the visible opposing species: against Tyranitar, Earthquake for Snorlax and Hydro Pump for Poliwrath; against Exeggutor, either Self-Destruct or Body Slam for Snorlax and Return for Poliwrath. The baseline uses the existing finite-horizon ledger. The support scheduler allocates work to every opponent reply, prioritizes favorable chance outcomes, and stops refining a branch once its lower mass exceeds 1e-8. Guided chance exploration tries valid script-prefix alternatives, retains distinct complete draw scripts with their actual product probabilities, and leaves all omitted mass unknown. It is not a Monte Carlo win-rate estimate or a favorable-outcome game model. All intervals are checked by the existing rational ledger verifier. A previously solved positive control, a one-execution unknown control, and corrupted-ledger rejection checks are included. Native guided support is separately tested as a submeasure of complete small kernels. Engine transitions, draw partitions and guarded identities remain trusted. This compact archive stores exact output digests and verification reports; --replay regenerates every full ledger, verifies it and compares all digests. A zero lower bound here is inconclusive about the policy value. Upper bounds apply only to each fixed continuation, not to unrestricted Switch play. The experiment does not tighten the game-value interval or justify a production change."
